        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.37,
          "en": "-: What are angular CLI schematics?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.37,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "Schematics are a powerful tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.31,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "or a concept introduced by the angular team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "or specifically by the angular CLI team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "Schematics are basically blueprints which certain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "angular commands can pick up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "And for example, you can have schematics for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 24.718,
          "en": "ng generate to generate new building blocks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.718,
          "end": 25.551,
          "en": "in your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.551,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "like components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 27.63,
          "en": "For ng add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.63,
          "end": 29.76,
          "en": "which we hadn't had a closer look at yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.76,
          "end": 31.2,
          "en": "for adding, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.2,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "libraries or certain capabilities to a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "and ng update for keeping your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 37.893,
          "en": "project up to date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 41.1,
          "en": "You can build your own schematics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.1,
          "end": 43.32,
          "en": "Angular has some built in schematics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.32,
          "end": 45.12,
          "en": "which you have unlocked by",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 45.12,
          "end": 46.92,
          "en": "default in the angular CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 46.92,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "And third party packages can also add schematics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 52.95,
          "en": "and that's what makes this feature powerful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 52.95,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "Now, adding your own schematics,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 56.55,
          "en": "of course, is super powerful because you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "could build your own blueprints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 61.2,
          "en": "your own ng generate command for generating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
